### 📊 Key Findings & Benchmarks
* **Indexing Time:** Lexical models (BM25, TF-IDF, LM) shared the fastest indexing time at **1.432 seconds**[span_7](start_span)[span_7](end_span). Among dense models, `Vector_Silm` took **25.741 seconds**, making it roughly **9.8x faster** to build than `Vector_E5` (251.588 seconds)[span_8](start_span)[span_8](end_span).
* **Query Latency:** `LM` achieved the fastest average query time (**2.254 ms**)[span_9](start_span)[span_9](end_span). For semantic models, `Vector_Silm` was significantly faster (**13.922 ms**) compared to `Vector_E5` (**77.118 ms**)[span_10](start_span)[span_10](end_span).
* **Coverage:** Dense vector models (`Vector_E5` and `Vector_Silm`) successfully returned top results for all 8 queries (including English and misspelled ones), whereas lexical models excelled at precise keyword matching but lacked coverage on out-of-vocabulary or semantic queries[span_11](start_span)[span_11](end_span).

